src-tauri/target/
*.png
src-tauri/gen/schemas/
!docs/ref-shots/**/*.png
# recon evidence for R34 (title rename): the shots ARE the measurement — a
# prose claim about a focus ring is not verifiable, the pixels are.
!docs/recon-title-rename/**/*.png
# recon evidence for scroll-sync: the shots carry the L<NNNN> markers the whole
# measurement is read from — measure.sh re-derives every number from these pngs.
!docs/recon-scroll-sync/**/*.png
dist/
.cov-evidence/

# per-worktree goal state (display, HOME, TMPDIR). Generated by scripts/wt.sh.
# NEVER tracked: a committed .goalenv merges into another goal and `cd`s it
# into the WRONG worktree — that happened 2026-09-12 (drop-attach -> main ->
# inline-title), which is how a goal ends up building in a peer's tree.
.goalenv
# recon-bmmenu: the stock 1.13.7 bookmark-row menu — the README reads every label off these
!docs/recon-bmmenu/**/*.png
# docs/palette-wasp/reference.png is the operator picture the wasp palette is traced to (criterion 1 of goal/wasp)
!docs/palette-wasp/reference.png
# recon-tabmenu: the stock 1.13.7 NOTE TAB menu. Every row count, box size and
# wording in docs/recon-tabmenu/README.md is read off these crops, so they are
# the measurement, not decoration. Without this exception the shots are silently
# ignored: iteration 3 reported "five shots committed" and `git ls-files` showed
# none — `git add` on an ignored path is a no-op that prints nothing.
!docs/recon-tabmenu/**/*.png

# recon-dotfiles: the evidence IS the deliverable — .gitignore line 2 (*.png)
# would otherwise keep every cited shot out of a clone (measured on themearch
# and on srclick: README cites a path a reviewer cannot open).
!docs/recon-dotfiles/**/*.png
# recon-srclick: acceptance criterion 1 is "every C1-C12 answer names a shot
# that EXISTS under docs/recon-srclick/shots/" — so these pngs are the evidence
# a reviewer opens, not incidental screenshots. The numbers beside them live in
# docs/recon-srclick/measurements/*.json (DOM state) and *-scroll.json (frames).
!docs/recon-srclick/**/*.png
# rvcursor: the pointer crops and masks ARE the measurement (criteria 2 and 5).
# A prose claim about a cursor shape is not verifiable; the pixels are, and the
# masks are what the classifier compares.
!docs/recon-rvcursor/**/*.png
!docs/negctl-rvcursor/**/*.png
# recon-flatpak: shots/ is the launch evidence for the goal's criterion 2 — a
# .flatpak that "launches" is a claim until the pixels are in the tree next to
# the census line that measured them (docs/recon-flatpak, item L).
!docs/recon-flatpak/**/*.png
# recon-tabclose: the S3 measurement — stock 1.13.7 ORPHANS the tab ("No file")
# on an external rename/delete instead of closing it. The title log alone cannot
# show that the tab is still in the strip; 11-ren-after.png and 21-del-after.png can.
!docs/recon-tabclose/shots/*.png
# recon-bmfolder: criterion 1 is "every answer names a committed shot it was
# read from" — group creation, the group row menu, indent geometry, delete and
# restart are all read off these pngs, so they are evidence, not screenshots.
!docs/recon-bmfolder/shots/*.png
# themecsp: the egress-proof evidence (shots ARE the deliverable, criterion 1-2)
!docs/themecsp/**/*.png
